      "credit": "King Leopold's Soliloquy: A Defense of His Congo Rule, By Mark Twain, Boston: The P. R. Warren Co., 1905, Second Edition.",
      "source": "MutilatedChildrenFromCongo",
      "description": "Mutilated Congolese children and adults (c. 1900-1905) — in Congo Free State (present-day Democratic Republic of the Congo)\nPrivately owned territory of Belgian King Leopold II, with numerous enslaved rubber collection/production areas in the rainforest and on plantations.\nRubber production used human rights abuses against the Congolese people, including amputations for unmet quotas and other colonial offenses.",
